    "declared": {
      "summary": "Build and qualify a new two-node net11 candidate graph with a source-free locked consumer, no publication.",
      "value": "RS339 succeeded first-pass under DWF 0.1.76 and retained incomplete C02 acceptance. RS340 builds a new unpublished two-node net11/C#15 Statistics and Quantities candidate in a disposable workspace from tracked copies of the actual source projects. Quantities is packed first; the copied Statistics project replaces its original project edge with an exact candidate package dependency, and is then packed. A separate source-free consumer restores only these two candidate archives into an isolated cache, locks the exact graph, checks package and binary identities, executes the existing twelve-check fixture and refuses a changed version under locked restore. Existing production files and immutable private packages are preserved. This is bounded candidate evidence, not production migration, publication, phase closure or universal compatibility.",
